The assessment is written and committed at cbbe515b (session_plan/assessment.md). I skipped the competitor research and the yopedia recall because I ran out of context during the survey, and the assessment says so.

State:
• **Health:** The build and tests are green, and the last 10 sessions each finished 2/2 with no reverts. CI is green, and the latest evolve runs succeeded.
• **Live checks:** I ran the binary from an empty folder with no config. `-p` and piped input both print exactly `PONG\n`, so the blank-line fixes from Day 215 hold outside the tests.

I reproduced the two issues the creator filed today:
• **#979:** I put a corrupted `.yoyo/last-session.json` in place and ran `-p … --continue`. It printed a warning, started a fresh conversation, called the model and exited 0, which is the silent restart the issue describes. The fix point is restore_session (src/main.rs:1010). It runs before the -p branch, so a strict mode can exit before any model call is made.
• #978: After a -p run, .yoyo/ holds only audit.jsonl, so no session is saved. The REPL is the only thing that calls auto_save_on_exit (repl.rs:1492), though that function already takes the target folder as a parameter.

Constraints for the planner:
• `cli.rs is registered at exactly its current length (7584) in tests/module_size.rs. Adding a flag means updating that entry or putting the logic in commands_session.rs`, which has room (1754 lines against the 2000 cap).
• New flags also have to be added to the known-flags list at cli.rs:693 and to help.rs.
• For #978, the agent has to call agent.finish().await before save_messages(), or the saved history is stale.
• The stream-json acknowledgement #979 asks for has to be printed by yoyo itself, because yoagent has no such event.

Suggested order: #979 first. Its key check is that plain --continue stays byte-for-byte unchanged. Then #978, which has to cover both -p and piped input. If either turns out too big, the fallback is the second half of #976: after a mid-stream failure, each retry re-prints the partial answer, so a pipe gets six copies.
